.TH TIGER 1 "August 2026" "xtiger 0.9" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tiger, tiger-term \- TI-92 emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tiger
[\fB\-r\fR \fIromfile\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fIcfgfile\fR]
.br
.B tiger-term
[\fB\-r\fR \fIromfile\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fIcfgfile\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tiger
emulates the Texas Instruments TI-92 graphing calculator. It draws the
calculator's LCD in a resizable window using SDL2, running natively under
either Wayland or X11.
.PP
.B tiger-term
is the same emulator rendering to a terminal instead, in 24-bit color,
using half-blocks, quadrants, sextants, or braille depending on how much
room the terminal has. It needs no display server.
.PP
A TI-92 ROM image is required and is not supplied with this program; see
.B FILES
below.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-r " romfile"
Use the specified ROM image instead of
.IR ti92.rom .
.TP
.BI \-c " cfgfile"
Use the specified config file instead of
.IR tiger.cfg .
.SH KEYS
Letters, digits, F1\-F8, the arrow keys and the usual arithmetic keys map
directly to their TI-92 equivalents. The calculator's modifier and
function keys are reached as follows:
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
l l.
Shift@SHIFT
Ctrl@DIAMOND
Alt@2ND
Caps Lock@HAND
Tab@STO>
Home@CLEAR
PageUp@MODE
Scroll Lock@ON
Insert@LN
Delete@SIN
End@COS
PageDown@TAN
F12@APPS
;@THETA
<@(\-) negate
.TE
.PP
.B F9
enters the built-in debugger,
.B F10
enters command mode, and
.B F11
quits.
.PP
Terminals report no key-release events, so under
.B tiger-term
a key reads as held for a short time after each press, and the modifiers
differ: an uppercase letter is SHIFT plus that letter, Alt plus a key is
2ND, and Ctrl plus a key is DIAMOND. Ctrl-O is ON, Ctrl-T cycles the
render mode, Ctrl-L forces a redraw, and Ctrl-Q quits.
.SH COMMAND MODE
Pressing F10 gives a prompt on the controlling terminal.
.B help
lists the available commands,
.B "load \fIfile\fB.92p"
sends a file to the emulated calculator over the link port, and
.B quit
returns to the emulator. Settings made here can be written to a config
file with
.BR putcfg .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ti92.rom
The ROM image, read from the current directory unless
.B \-r
says otherwise. ROM images are copyrighted by Texas Instruments and are
not distributed with this program; you must dump one from a calculator
you own.
.TP
.I ti92.mem
Machine state, written to the current directory on exit and reloaded at
startup.
.TP
.I tiger.cfg
Config file, read from the current directory unless
.B \-c
says otherwise.
.SH AUTHORS
Written by Jonas Minnberg and released under the GPL in 2001 by
Misha Nasledov, who has maintained it since. The 68k emulation core
derives from UAE.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tiemu (1)
.PP
This program is preserved rather than actively developed. TiEmu, which
descends from this codebase, is the more capable emulator for day-to-day
use.
